// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! A Bluetooth profile driver's two functions, after BeginIO and AbortIO:
//! what bluetooth.library calls a driver in DEVS:bluetooth/ with when it
//! offers it a service of a bonded device, and when it takes it back.
//! Every profile driver has them (sdk/devices/btprofile.zig); the base is
//! the driver's, io_Device of an open request.
##include libs/bluetooth/bluetooth as bluetooth
##interface
##basetype BTProfileBase
##name btprofile
##bias 6
##public
/// A service offered: true if the driver takes it - it has filled a
/// unit, `binding.unit` saying which, and keeps `binding` until
/// BTProfileUnbind - false if it declines and the next driver is asked.
/// Called on the library's binder process, which serves nothing else
/// meanwhile: the driver may call the library - read the service's
/// record, add listeners, open channels - and wait for it.
bool BTProfileBind(*bluetooth.BTBinding binding)
/// The service is taken back - its controller gone, or its bond ended
/// (BTPU_FORGET in `flags`, for the driver to tell the device first,
/// while the link is there): its channels closed, its unit left without
/// it, `binding` no longer the driver's. Called on the binder process.
void BTProfileUnbind(*bluetooth.BTBinding binding, u32 flags)
##end
